  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1031 PM CDT Wed Oct 14 2026\n\nThe cold front that lags behind the rain we saw today is expected to \nswing through on Friday. This frontal passage looks to be dry, with \nthe exception of some low rain chances on the Cumberland Plateau. \nAfter this, we're not expecting any rain for the remainder of the \nforecast period. Overall, we're looking at highs in the 60s/70s and \nlows in the 30s and 40s for the weekend. Our temperatures will drop \nso much that we could see our first frost of the season on the \nCumberland Plateau on Sunday morning. Sadly, it will only be a taste \nof fall, as the return of clearer skies will also bring back the \nheat. Highs by mid-week next week will creep back up into the upper \n70s.",
